	🚪 I. THE EXPORT CONVENIENCE STORY
As a Sovereign Operator, when I select a single Advocate inside the Persona Center (Advocate Center) and click "Export MD" or "Export JSON," I want the browser's download prompt to automatically populate the default filename with the selected advocate's username (e.g., mando_enforcer_export.md or mando_enforcer_export.json) instead of forcing the generic sovereign_personas_export.md fallback.


If multiple Advocate records are selected, this dynamic naming logic must not apply, and the system must gracefully fall back to the generic sovereign_personas_export.md string. This prevents filename chaos during batch operations while delivering high-speed convenience during single-Advocate archiving.


This aligns with our commitment to absolute efficiency under the Sovereign OS Canonical Lexicon Version 2.0 standard.
⚙️ II. FRONTEND TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION
To implement this dynamic name check, the file export action triggers inside PersonaCenter.tsx (the React component managing your active Advocate card grids) must be patched to conditionally check the length of selected items.
Existing Deficient State:
Currently, the download helper is hardcoded to a static export string:const blob = new Blob([mdContent], { type: "text/markdown" });


const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);


const a = document.createElement("a");


a.href = url;


a.download = "sovereign_personas_export.md"; // Hardcoded static name


a.click();
Proposed Resolution State:
Refactor the export click handler in PersonaCenter.tsx to resolve the selected advocate's username dynamically:const handleExportMD = () => {


  if (selectedIds.length === 0) return;


  const selectedAdvocates = personas.filter(p => selectedIds.includes(p.sys_id));


  const mdContent = generateMDContent(selectedAdvocates);





  const blob = new Blob([mdContent], { type: "text/markdown" });


  const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);


  const a = document.createElement("a");


  a.href = url;





  // Conditionally assign the download filename based on selection count


  a.download = selectedAdvocates.length === 1 


    ? `${selectedAdvocates[0].user_name}_export.md` 


    : "sovereign_personas_export.md";





  document.body.appendChild(a);


  a.click();


  document.body.removeChild(a);


  URL.revokeObjectURL(url);


};


Apply the identical conditional logic to the handleExportJSON action handler to dynamically output ${selectedAdvocates[0].user_name}_export.json upon single selections.
